Edumart — Full Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Scope: Greenfield development, from product discovery and system design through implementation, security, testing, deployment, and post-launch scaling.

The objective is to build Edumart as a production-grade education platform, not simply an MVP that will need to be rebuilt when usage grows.

The PRD will cover the complete product lifecycle: the initial launch, subsequent feature releases, institutional adoption, monetization, platform reliability, and long-term expansion.
Product direction
Edumart will bring together five connected product areas:
1. Learning and examination preparation — JAMB/UTME, WAEC, NECO, Post-UTME, practice questions, timed examinations, explanations, and performance tracking.
2. Classroom and institutional management — teachers, classes, cohorts, invitations, assessments, student progress, and institutional reporting.
3. Digital publications and marketplace — educational books, learning resources, publisher listings, purchases, and controlled access to digital content.
4. Rewards and referrals — learning points, streaks, achievements, referral attribution, and separately managed eligible monetary commissions.
5. Platform administration and insights — content moderation, user and institution management, payment reconciliation, analytics, support tools, security auditing, and operational monitoring.
The platform will launch as a mobile-first Progressive Web App (PWA), with native mobile applications considered later. The architecture should support growth without introducing distributed-system complexity before it is justified.
