22. Production launch checklist
Do not launch until the accountable owners can verify that:
- [ ] Product and design owners accept the critical user journeys.
- [ ] Authentication and privileged access have been reviewed.
- [ ] Protected endpoints enforce authorization and tenant boundaries.
- [ ] Exam writes are idempotent and server-acknowledged.
- [ ] Submission and scoring are reproducible.
- [ ] Payment processing, if enabled, uses verified provider state and reconciliation.
- [ ] Content provenance and rights are documented.
- [ ] Required terms, privacy notices, refund policies, and support channels are published.
- [ ] Critical security findings are closed.
- [ ] Backups, point-in-time recovery, and restoration have been tested.
- [ ] Monitoring, alerting, incident response, and deployment recovery are operational.
- [ ] Load tests meet the agreed concurrent-exam target.
- [ ] Support staff have playbooks for access problems, exam disputes, payment mismatches, content complaints, and suspected fraud.
- [ ] The release owner has signed off on known risks and outstanding limitations.
23. Post-launch operating model
Daily during controlled launch: review errors, exam-save failures, submission failures, payment mismatches, security alerts, and support volume.

Weekly: review activation, retention, learning engagement, content quality, institution adoption, and operating cost.

Monthly: review backup evidence, access permissions, dependency updates, and incident trends.

Quarterly: conduct a disaster-recovery exercise, privacy and retention review, and architecture/cost assessment.

