2. Product Requirements Document (PRD)
2.1 Problem statement
Students often prepare using disconnected materials and lack reliable feedback about weak topics or exam readiness. Teachers need a practical way to assign assessments and review class performance. Institutions need consistent assessment workflows and visibility. Publishers and educational creators need a trusted way to distribute legitimate materials. Edumart brings these jobs into one product while preserving clear permissions and auditable commerce.
2.2 Product goals
1.	Help a new student complete a first useful practice session quickly, ideally in the first visit after onboarding.
2.	Deliver correct, explainable, recoverable assessments with server-authoritative timing and scoring.
3.	Let a teacher create a class, invite students and run a scheduled assessment without manual result compilation.
4.	Provide students and teachers with meaningful progress insights, not decorative dashboards.
5.	Support legitimate paid educational content with reliable payment confirmation and entitlement enforcement.
6.	Implement reward mechanics that are transparent, fraud-resistant and financially auditable.
7.	Establish production operations: monitoring, backups, restore tests, support workflows, access controls and incident response.
