Build this before broad parallel feature work: student registers → chooses a subject/topic → receives approved questions → submits an answer → sees explanation/score → result persists → student returns and sees history. This validates the web/API/database contract, authorization, content lifecycle and learning loop in one thin end-to-end path.
9.3 Definition of ready / done
•	Ready: user problem and acceptance criteria are clear; design/state cases exist; data/permission implications reviewed; API contract agreed; dependencies identified.
•	Done: code reviewed; tests added; accessibility/responsive behavior checked; logs/metrics added for critical path; migrations reviewed; documentation/runbook updated; feature works in staging; product owner accepts.
•	A ticket is not done because the happy path works on one developer’s machine.
•	Every production bug has severity, impact, reproduction, root cause or investigation owner, and a regression test when feasible.
