18. Final engineering principles
48.	Correctness before breadth: make the assessment loop dependable before adding many modules.
49.	Content quality is a product feature. Treat provenance, review and correction as core workflows.
50.	Server-side authority: permissions, time, scores, price, payment and reward eligibility are not frontend responsibilities.
51.	Make retries safe: network failures are normal; idempotency is a design requirement.
52.	Separate ledgers and state machines. Avoid ambiguous balance fields and overloaded status columns.
53.	Design for operations: every important failure needs visibility, ownership and a recovery path.
54.	Ship a modular monolith with clear boundaries, then split only when evidence justifies it.
55.	Measure real learning and business outcomes; do not optimize vanity metrics.
56.	Keep the PWA lean and accessible; add native apps when measured user needs warrant them.
57.	Document decisions and teach the team the invariants, not just the code structure.
